# Folkprotocol Tone v0
#
# Sixth experimental slice. Claude Sonnet 4.5 diagnoses the factual draft,
# rewrites it, and then performs a separate local prose review. It may not do
# research or change the factual record.

Expect slug
Default work_dir: /home/patrick/projects/folkprotocol

Work in {work_dir}

CC: """Create a tone brief for
research/source-maps/{slug}/100-factual-draft.md.

Verify that 100-factual-draft.md ends with its completion marker. Also read
00-commission.md and 80-practice-assessment.md for purpose and editorial
choices. From research/source-maps/{slug}/ compute the input digest with exactly
`sha256sum 00-commission.md 80-practice-assessment.md 100-factual-draft.md |
sha256sum`. Write that digest as inputDigest in the YAML frontmatter of
research/source-maps/{slug}/110-tone-brief.md. If an existing tone brief ends
with `TONE BRIEF COMPLETE` and records the same digest, leave it unchanged.
Read no other files, do no web research, and write only 110-tone-brief.md. Work
yourself: do not delegate, spawn subagents, or start another agent workflow.

Diagnose the draft at sentence and section level. The desired voice is a
knowledgeable, curious person who has actually looked through the territory and
can make judgments without posing as a clinician. It is warm through attention
and specificity, not through chummy filler. It can say a direction is thin,
strange, disputed, commercially inflated, or worth trying when that is the
record. It does not make published trials the default ruler for every other
kind of knowledge.

Identify concrete instances of:

- report voice, academic scaffolding, or source-method narration left in prose
- medical-site habits: scolding, generic safety throat-clearing, reflexive
  abstinence, `talk to your doctor`, or facile individual-variation caveats
- evidence-status tics: repeating `limited evidence`, treating PubMed as the
  court of appeal, or calling anything without an RCT merely anecdotal
- assistant tics: symmetrical lists, canned transitions, repeated mini-verdicts,
  `promising`, `classic`, `may help`, and overexplaining obvious things
- false warmth, sales language, wellness copy, or imitation of the commissioner
- places where qualifications swamp the actual observation
- places where the draft hides its useful judgment or functional effect size
- laundry-list structure, especially around supplements

For each problem quote a short identifying phrase, explain what it does to the
voice, and give a local rewrite direction. Also identify passages whose voice
should be preserved. Do not rewrite the page in this pass. End with
`TONE BRIEF COMPLETE`.""" model=claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929, timeout=1200

Then CC: """Rewrite
research/source-maps/{slug}/100-factual-draft.md using
research/source-maps/{slug}/110-tone-brief.md. Write only
research/source-maps/{slug}/120-tone-draft.md.

This is a prose transformation, not a new research pass. Read the factual draft
and tone brief only. From research/source-maps/{slug}/ compute the input digest
with exactly `sha256sum 100-factual-draft.md 110-tone-brief.md | sha256sum`.
Write that digest as inputDigest in the output YAML. If a 120-tone-draft.md ends
with its completion marker, records the same digest, and its prose above
`## References` is at most 5,500 words, leave it unchanged. Work yourself: do
not delegate, spawn subagents, or start another agent workflow. Preserve every
factual claim, number, preparation detail,
timing, uncertainty, source-type distinction, citation token, reference entry,
YAML field, and the final reference count. Do not add facts from memory, remove
thin or strange directions, strengthen conclusions, or make a new protocol.

Apply the brief locally rather than flattening the whole page into one house
style. Prefer concrete sentences and paragraphs over repeated labels or tables.
Keep useful judgments visible. Do not add generic warnings, evidence apologies,
obvious convenience commentary, quantified-self homework, faux-folksy language,
or a moral about drinking. Do not imitate profanity.

Set YAML `tonePass: claude-sonnet-4.5-v0`. Replace the final completion marker with
`TONE DRAFT COMPLETE — N references`, preserving the true unique-reference
count. Count only prose above `## References` with awk and keep that prose at
most 5,500 words; reference entries do not count against the prose cap.""" model=claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929, inherit_previous_output=false, timeout=1800

Then CC: """Review the completed tone draft against the factual
draft and tone brief. Read only 100-factual-draft.md, 110-tone-brief.md, and
120-tone-draft.md. Solely for the idempotency check below, you may inspect the
existing 121-tone-review.md frontmatter inputDigest and final marker; do not
read or reuse its findings. From research/source-maps/{slug}/ compute the input digest
with exactly `sha256sum 100-factual-draft.md 110-tone-brief.md
120-tone-draft.md | sha256sum`. Write that digest as inputDigest in the YAML
frontmatter of research/source-maps/{slug}/121-tone-review.md. If an existing
review ends with `TONE REVIEW COMPLETE` and records the same digest, leave it
unchanged. Do not edit the draft. Write only 121-tone-review.md. Work yourself:
do not delegate, spawn subagents, or start another agent workflow.

Report concrete remaining tone failures with an identifying phrase and a local
repair. Also report any factual claim, number, citation, reference, preparation,
or qualification that the rewrite added, removed, or changed. Do not propose a
new structure or re-litigate the factual content. Do not suggest removing a
useful effect size, exact community amount, source-access boundary, population
limit, or material qualification merely to make prose smoother. Do not turn a
failed search into proof of absence or replace an observational result with a
causal claim. Source-kind language is appropriate where it tells the reader
what kind of record an amount or claim comes from. If there are no concrete
tone or fidelity defects, write `CLEAN`. End with `TONE REVIEW COMPLETE`.""" model=claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929, inherit_previous_output=false, timeout=1200
